{"id":14119,"artist":"H.Tucker. Seq","title":"Sweet Genevieve","lyrics_plain":null,"lyrics_synced":"[00:15.56] O, Genevieve I'd give the world\n[00:18.89] To live again the lovely past!\n[00:22.22] The rose of youth was dew~impearled;\n[00:25.56] But now it withers in the blast.\n[00:29.17] I see thy face in ev'ry dream,\n[00:32.23] My waking thoughts are full of thee;\n[00:35.84] Thy glance is in the starry beam\n[00:38.89] That falls along the Summer sea.\n[00:42.78] O Genevieve, Sweet Genevieve,\n[00:46.78] The days may come, the days may go,\n[00:50.24] But still the hands of mem'ry weave\n[00:54.23] The blissful dreams of long ago.\n[01:11.54] Fair Genevieve, my early love,\n[01:15.00] The years but make thee dearer far!\n[01:18.47] My heart shall never rove:\n[01:21.93] Thou art my only guiding star,\n[01:25.68] For me the past has no regret\n[01:28.85] Whate'er the years may bring to me;\n[01:32.60] I bless the hour when first we met,\n[01:35.77] The hour that gave me love and thee!\n[01:39.77] O Genevieve, Sweet Genevieve,\n[01:43.76] The days may come, the days may go,\n[01:47.23] But still the hands of mem'ry weave\n[01:51.22] The blissful dreams of long ago.\n[01:54.68] O, Genevieve!\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:15.55] <00:15.55>O, <00:16.11>Gen <00:16.52>ev <00:16.66>ieve <00:17.22>I'd <00:17.77>give <00:18.19>the <00:18.33>world\n[00:18.89] <00:18.89>To <00:19.44>live <00:19.86>a <00:20.00>gain <00:20.55>the <00:21.11>lo <00:21.29>v <00:21.48>ely <00:21.66>past!\n[00:22.22] <00:22.22>The <00:22.77>rose <00:23.19>of <00:23.33>youth <00:23.89>was <00:24.44>dew <00:24.86>~im <00:25.00>pearled;\n[00:25.55] <00:25.55>But <00:26.11>now <00:26.53>it <00:26.66>with <00:26.94>ers <00:27.78>in <00:28.19>the <00:28.33>blast.\n[00:29.16] <00:29.16>I <00:29.44>see <00:29.72>thy <00:30.00>face <00:30.55>in <00:31.11>ev <00:31.39>'ry <00:31.66>dream,\n[00:32.22] <00:32.22>My <00:32.78>wa <00:33.05>king <00:33.33>thoughts <00:33.89>are <00:34.44>full <00:34.72>of <